---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
---
<Layout title="Finance hire or Finable? One finance hire or a complete finance team | Finable" description="You're looking for one finance professional. But the work often calls for a complete finance team. Compare an internal finance hire with a Finable finance team.">
<div style="max-width:100%;overflow-x:hidden;background:var(--white)">

  <Header />

  <!-- HERO (navy, single column: typography is the visual) -->
  <section class="hero-navy" style="background:var(--navy)">
    <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:72px">
    <div class="hero" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:clamp(36px,4.6vw,68px);align-items:center">
      <div>
        <div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:26px">Considering a finance hire?</div>
        <h1 style="font-size:clamp(36px,4.6vw,58px);line-height:1.05;margin-bottom:26px">You're looking for one finance professional. <span class="em">You may need a finance team.</span></h1>
        <p style="font-size:clamp(16px,1.6vw,19px);color:rgba(255,255,255,.78);max-width:560px;text-wrap:pretty">Behind one vacancy there is often work of several kinds: day-to-day finance, month-end close, controlling, reporting, and cash and forecast. Sometimes that fits one employee. Sometimes it calls for several areas of expertise side by side.</p>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:16px 28px;margin-top:34px">
          <Button href="#alternative">See the alternative &rarr;</Button>
          <a href="/en/book-a-call" style="font-weight:600;font-size:16px;color:var(--terracotta)">Discuss your finance vacancy &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><div class="rule"></div></div>

  <!-- THE ROLE -->
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:72px">
    <div class="split" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 1px minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(40px,5vw,72px);align-items:start">
      <div>
        <div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:22px">The role</div>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,36px);margin-bottom:26px">It often starts with one job description.</h2>
        <div>
          <div class="cat">Accounting</div>
          <div class="chk"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--navy)">Oversee the financial administration</span></div>
          <div class="cat" style="margin-top:16px">Financial control</div>
          <div class="chk"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--navy)">Run the month-end close</span></div>
          <div class="chk"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--navy)">Review the numbers and explain variances</span></div>
          <div class="chk"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--navy)">Monitor cash flow and working capital</span></div>
          <div class="cat" style="margin-top:16px">Reporting &amp; planning</div>
          <div class="chk"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--navy)">Prepare management reports</span></div>
          <div class="chk"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--navy)">Build budgets and forecasts</span></div>
          <div class="cat" style="margin-top:16px">Business control</div>
          <div class="chk"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--navy)">Advise management based on the numbers</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="vdiv" style="background:var(--line)"></div>
      <div class="reveal" style="padding-top:44px">
        <div style="width:44px;height:2px;background:var(--terracotta);margin-bottom:24px"></div>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(28px,3.4vw,42px);line-height:1.14;margin-bottom:24px">That's not just one role.<br>That's a finance function.</h2>
        <p style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body);max-width:520px;text-wrap:pretty">What starts as one vacancy often combines accounting, financial control, reporting and business control. That does not mean one employee is unsuitable: it depends on the volume per area and on the level you need in each. It is the question worth answering before you start recruiting.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><div class="rule"></div></div>

  <!-- THE DECISION -->
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:72px">
    <div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:22px">The decision</div>
    <h2 style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.2vw,38px);margin-bottom:40px">One finance hire or a complete finance team?</h2>

    <!-- Mobile (≤639): the same comparison, topic by topic. -->
    <div class="cmp-m">
      <div class="cmp-m-pair"><div class="cmp-m-dim">Expertise and capacity</div><div class="cmp-m-row"><span class="cmp-m-k">One finance hire</span><span class="cmp-m-v">One profile with one person&rsquo;s hours. You can widen it by working with your bookkeeper, accountant or a specialist.</span></div><div class="cmp-m-row is-fin"><span class="cmp-m-k">Finable</span><span class="cmp-m-v">Several areas of expertise within one team. The capacity is agreed, not unlimited.</span></div></div>
      <div class="cmp-m-pair"><div class="cmp-m-dim">Direction and collaboration</div><div class="cmp-m-row"><span class="cmp-m-k">One finance hire</span><span class="cmp-m-v">You direct the work yourself, day by day and close at hand, and set the priorities.</span></div><div class="cmp-m-row is-fin"><span class="cmp-m-k">Finable</span><span class="cmp-m-v">You steer on agreements through one fixed point of contact in the Netherlands. The delivery team works from India.</span></div></div>
      <div class="cmp-m-pair"><div class="cmp-m-dim">Continuity and cover</div><div class="cmp-m-row"><span class="cmp-m-k">One finance hire</span><span class="cmp-m-v">During holidays, illness or a resignation you have to place the work elsewhere for a while.</span></div><div class="cmp-m-row is-fin"><span class="cmp-m-k">Finable</span><span class="cmp-m-v">The work is spread across a team, so you depend less on one person. That does require documented processes and transferable knowledge.</span></div></div>
      <div class="cmp-m-pair"><div class="cmp-m-dim">Cost structure</div><div class="cmp-m-row"><span class="cmp-m-k">One finance hire</span><span class="cmp-m-v">Salary, employer costs and recruitment. A fixed cost, whatever the volume.</span></div><div class="cmp-m-row is-fin"><span class="cmp-m-k">Finable</span><span class="cmp-m-v">One monthly fee based on scope, volume and complexity. Which option works out cheaper depends on your situation.</span></div></div>
      <div class="cmp-m-pair"><div class="cmp-m-dim">Onboarding and handover</div><div class="cmp-m-row"><span class="cmp-m-k">One finance hire</span><span class="cmp-m-v">Recruiting, onboarding and building up knowledge takes time from your own organisation.</span></div><div class="cmp-m-row is-fin"><span class="cmp-m-k">Finable</span><span class="cmp-m-v">The team is already in place, but still has to learn your business, processes and systems. That asks something of you too.</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cmp" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,0.9fr);gap:clamp(24px,3vw,44px);align-items:start">
      <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:30px 32px">
        <h3 style="font-size:21px;margin-bottom:18px">One finance hire</h3>
        <div class="cmp-row"><span class="cmp-dim">Expertise and capacity</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--body)">One profile with one person&rsquo;s hours. You can widen it by working with your bookkeeper, accountant or a specialist.</span></div>
        <div class="cmp-row"><span class="cmp-dim">Direction and collaboration</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--body)">You direct the work yourself, day by day and close at hand, and set the priorities.</span></div>
        <div class="cmp-row"><span class="cmp-dim">Continuity and cover</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--body)">During holidays, illness or a resignation you have to place the work elsewhere for a while.</span></div>
        <div class="cmp-row"><span class="cmp-dim">Cost structure</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--body)">Salary, employer costs and recruitment. A fixed cost, whatever the volume.</span></div>
        <div class="cmp-row"><span class="cmp-dim">Onboarding and handover</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--body)">Recruiting, onboarding and building up knowledge takes time from your own organisation.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div style="border:1px solid rgba(196,100,58,0.22);border-radius:12px;padding:30px 32px;background:var(--terracotta-soft)">
        <h3 style="font-size:21px;margin-bottom:18px;color:var(--terracotta)">Finable</h3>
        <div class="cmp-row" style="border-color:rgba(27,58,92,0.1)"><span class="cmp-dim">Expertise and capacity</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--navy)">Several areas of expertise within one team. The capacity is agreed, not unlimited.</span></div>
        <div class="cmp-row" style="border-color:rgba(27,58,92,0.1)"><span class="cmp-dim">Direction and collaboration</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--navy)">You steer on agreements through one fixed point of contact in the Netherlands. The delivery team works from India.</span></div>
        <div class="cmp-row" style="border-color:rgba(27,58,92,0.1)"><span class="cmp-dim">Continuity and cover</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--navy)">The work is spread across a team, so you depend less on one person. That does require documented processes and transferable knowledge.</span></div>
        <div class="cmp-row" style="border-color:rgba(27,58,92,0.1)"><span class="cmp-dim">Cost structure</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--navy)">One monthly fee based on scope, volume and complexity. Which option works out cheaper depends on your situation.</span></div>
        <div class="cmp-row" style="border-color:rgba(27,58,92,0.1)"><span class="cmp-dim">Onboarding and handover</span><span class="cmp-val" style="color:var(--navy)">The team is already in place, but still has to learn your business, processes and systems. That asks something of you too.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div style="padding-top:6px">
        <div style="width:44px;height:2px;background:var(--terracotta);margin-bottom:22px"></div>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(24px,2.8vw,34px);line-height:1.15;margin-bottom:20px">The finance expertise you need. In one team.</h2>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--body);text-wrap:pretty;margin-bottom:24px">Finable takes over agreed finance work, with one point of contact and a monthly fee that matches the scope, the volume and the complexity.</p>
        <Button href="/en/estimate" size="sm">Get an estimate &rarr;</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE ALTERNATIVE · NAVY ANCHOR -->
  <section id="alternative" style="background:var(--navy)">
    <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:76px;padding-bottom:76px">
      <div class="lbl" style="color:var(--terracotta);margin-bottom:20px">The alternative</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(28px,3.4vw,42px);color:var(--white);margin-bottom:48px">The parts you agree on. In one team.</h2>
      <div class="navy-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;gap:clamp(36px,4vw,64px);align-items:center">
        <div class="flow">
          <div>
            <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.5" style="margin-bottom:14px" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="4" width="18" height="24" rx="2"/><path d="M11 10h10M11 15h10M11 20h6"/></svg>
            <h3 style="font-size:15px;color:var(--white);margin-bottom:8px;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-weight:600">Daily finance</h3>
            <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--on-dark-secondary);line-height:1.55">The recurring work that keeps finance running.</p>
          </div>
          <svg class="fa" width="24" height="14" viewBox="0 0 30 18" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 9h24M18 2l8 7-8 7"/></svg>
          <div>
            <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.5" style="margin-bottom:14px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 8h20M6 8v18h20V8M6 8V5h20v3"/><path d="M11 14l3 3 6-6"/></svg>
            <h3 style="font-size:15px;color:var(--white);margin-bottom:8px;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-weight:600">Month-end close</h3>
            <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--on-dark-secondary);line-height:1.55">Closing each month in a structured and reliable way.</p>
          </div>
          <svg class="fa" width="24" height="14" viewBox="0 0 30 18" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 9h24M18 2l8 7-8 7"/></svg>
          <div>
            <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.5" style="margin-bottom:14px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 27h22"/><rect x="7" y="17" width="4" height="7"/><rect x="14" y="11" width="4" height="13"/><rect x="21" y="14" width="4" height="10"/></svg>
            <h3 style="font-size:15px;color:var(--white);margin-bottom:8px;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-weight:600">Controlling</h3>
            <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--on-dark-secondary);line-height:1.55">Reviewing performance, cash flow and variances.</p>
          </div>
          <svg class="fa" width="24" height="14" viewBox="0 0 30 18" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 9h24M18 2l8 7-8 7"/></svg>
          <div>
            <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.5" style="margin-bottom:14px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 4h12l6 6v18H8z"/><path d="M19 4v7h7"/><path d="M12 18l3 3 5-6"/></svg>
            <h3 style="font-size:15px;color:var(--white);margin-bottom:8px;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-weight:600">Reporting &amp; insight</h3>
            <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--on-dark-secondary);line-height:1.55">Turning the numbers into useful information for management.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;border-left:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);padding-left:clamp(24px,3vw,44px)">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--white);font-weight:500">A fixed team</span></div>
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--white);font-weight:500">One point of contact</span></div>
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5"/><path d="M6 10l2.5 2.5L14 7"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--white);font-weight:500">One fixed monthly fee</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="height:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.14);margin:48px 0 30px"></div>
      <p style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(20px,2.3vw,28px);color:var(--white);max-width:760px;text-wrap:balance">The right expertise for each part. One team and one point of contact.</p>
      <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--on-dark-secondary);margin-top:18px;max-width:760px;text-wrap:pretty">That includes watching cash and keeping the forecast up to date. You choose which parts Finable runs; the rest stays where it is today.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE SPLIT — what stays internal and what Finable runs. No new guarantees: this is the
       agreement made before the start, not a standard package. -->
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top:72px;padding-bottom:72px">
    <div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:22px">The split</div>
    <h2 style="font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,36px);margin-bottom:12px">What stays with you, what Finable takes over?</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body);max-width:700px;margin-bottom:40px;text-wrap:pretty">That differs per company. One client places a single part with Finable, another most of the day-to-day finance. What is fixed is where the line sits.</p>
    <div class="split" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 1px minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(40px,5vw,72px);align-items:start">
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,23px);margin-bottom:20px">Finable carries out</h3>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">The work you agree on together, with the responsibility that comes with it set out in advance</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">The preparation of the figures, reports and forecast you base your decisions on</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">Flagging what stands out in the numbers and what it means for the month ahead</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vdiv" style="background:var(--line)"></div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,23px);margin-bottom:20px">You keep</h3>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">Strategic choices, budget decisions and the approvals you have agreed on</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">The work you deliberately keep in-house, with your own people</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">The relationship with your bookkeeper, accountant or CFO, who can stay involved</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body);max-width:760px;margin-top:clamp(32px,3.4vw,44px);padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);text-wrap:pretty">Before the start we set out who does what, who gets which access, which checks are part of the work and how we work together. If the situation changes, the split changes with it.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><div class="rule"></div></div>

  <!-- WHEN EACH OPTION FITS -->
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top:72px;padding-bottom:72px">
    <div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:22px">When each option fits</div>
    <div class="split" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 1px minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(40px,5vw,72px);align-items:start">
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(22px,2.5vw,30px);margin-bottom:26px">Finable may be a better fit when&hellip;</h2>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">You need expertise in several areas, but a full role in none of them</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">Complexity is growing: more entities, more volume, more stakeholders asking for figures</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">Continuity matters more to you than proximity</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">You don't want to build a complete internal finance team yet</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vdiv" style="background:var(--line)"></div>
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(22px,2.5vw,30px);margin-bottom:26px">An internal hire may be a better fit when&hellip;</h2>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">There is enough work for one clearly defined, full role</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">Finance is interwoven with sales, operations or production day by day</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">A lot of the work is on site, or close to the people on the floor</span></div>
        <div class="chk"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#C4643A" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4L16 6"/></svg><span style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body)">You want to build finance in-house and recruit, manage and develop it yourself</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:var(--body);max-width:760px;margin-top:clamp(32px,3.4vw,44px);padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);text-wrap:pretty">A combination also happens: someone internal for the work that has to sit close by, and Finable for the parts that call for expertise or continuity. The question is not whether outsourcing or hiring is better, but which setup fits the finance work your organisation actually needs.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><div class="rule"></div></div>

  <!-- FAQ + TIM (navy) -->
  <section class="faq-navy" style="background:var(--navy)">
    <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:68px;padding-bottom:72px">
    <div class="end" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.1fr) 1px minmax(0,0.9fr);gap:clamp(40px,5vw,68px);align-items:start">
      <div>
        <div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:26px">Frequently asked questions</div>
        <details class="fin-faq"><summary><span class="fin-faq-q">Can Finable replace a finance hire?</span><span class="fin-faq-ic"></span></summary><div class="fin-faq-a"><p>Sometimes, sometimes not. It depends on the work behind the vacancy, not on the job title: the same title covers mostly bookkeeping at one company and mostly controlling and reporting at another. If that work calls for several kinds of expertise, a team is often a more logical answer than one broad role. If there is structurally enough work for one full internal role, hiring someone fits better. So we start with the work and the volume, and only then with the form.</p></div></details>
        <details class="fin-faq"><summary><span class="fin-faq-q">What if we want to hire someone later?</span><span class="fin-faq-ic"></span></summary><div class="fin-faq-a"><p>That's possible. Your finance setup doesn't have to stay the same forever. As your organisation grows, responsibilities can move in-house or the Finable scope can change. The aim is to organise finance around what the business needs at each stage.</p></div></details>
        <details class="fin-faq"><summary><span class="fin-faq-q">Who actually does the work?</span><span class="fin-faq-ic"></span></summary><div class="fin-faq-a"><p>The work is handled by finance professionals within the Finable team. Different responsibilities can be handled by different people depending on the expertise required, while you maintain one clear point of contact.</p></div></details>
        <details class="fin-faq"><summary><span class="fin-faq-q">How much capacity do we get?</span><span class="fin-faq-ic"></span></summary><div class="fin-faq-a"><p>Finable isn't sold as a fixed number of employee hours. We agree on the finance scope and organise the team around the work required to deliver it. The exact setup depends on the workload and complexity of your organisation.</p></div></details>
        <details class="fin-faq"><summary><span class="fin-faq-q">Does Finable work in our existing systems?</span><span class="fin-faq-ic"></span></summary><div class="fin-faq-a"><p>Where possible, yes. We first look at the systems and processes you already use. What works can stay. If changes would materially improve the finance operation, we'll discuss them as part of the setup.</p></div></details>
        <details class="fin-faq"><summary><span class="fin-faq-q">What happens if someone is ill or on holiday?</span><span class="fin-faq-ic"></span></summary><div class="fin-faq-a"><p>Because the work is organised across a team, you're less dependent on the availability of one individual. That only works where processes are documented and knowledge is transferable, which is part of the setup rather than something that happens by itself.</p></div></details>
        <details class="fin-faq"><summary><span class="fin-faq-q">When is hiring someone internally the better option?</span><span class="fin-faq-ic"></span></summary><div class="fin-faq-a"><p>An internal hire can be the better choice when you have enough work for a clearly defined full-time role, need someone deeply embedded in the organisation every day or want to build and manage the finance function internally.</p></div></details>
      </div>
